# Build steward rule

> `.cursor/rules/do-not-touch.mdc` (alwaysApply) is the floor — it applies above this
> rule. This file adds build/config-specific constraints on top of that floor.

## Read first

- `docs/DO_NOT_TOUCH.md`

## Must avoid

- Editing `next.config.ts` — CSP headers and redirects are locked.
- Editing `package.json` scripts.
- Editing `prisma.config.ts`.
- Editing the `provider = "..."` line in `prisma/schema.prisma` — it is build-swapped
  by `scripts/prisma-provider.mjs` (`PRISMA_PROVIDER=postgresql|sqlite`). Never hand-edit
  it for prod (sqlite local ↔ postgresql CI/Vercel).
- Editing Turbopack aliases or `tsconfig.json` paths.

## Validate before done

- `pnpm typecheck` always.
- `pnpm build` if any config file is touched (catches CSP / alias / provider regressions).
- Env keys are read via `process.env.X`, validated by the Zod `serverEnvSchema` in
  `src/lib/env.ts` (`export const env`). Flag any key NOT in the schema — e.g.
  `RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `OUTREACH_FROM` — before relying on it.

## STOP and ask before

- All of the above are DO_NOT_TOUCH locked zones. Propose a diff only — do **not** edit
  CSP / redirects / package scripts / `prisma.config.ts` / the schema provider line /
  Turbopack aliases / `tsconfig.json` without explicit approval.

## Priority

P0 (locked)
